      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To be fair, if you select the hips and two legs in edit mode and scale them to 0 on the Y (depth) axis it will neutralize their rotations and line them up (for a typical humanoid).\nThis will move the bones position, but it will reset their angle (to either 180 or 0 depending on the hips)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-03-18T00:46:49.432Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I've been having quite the frustration for some time now regarding the SDK's armature check system when it comes to bone angles and rotations. I'd love to see added the exact angle/rotation direction of the bone(x,y,z). Because I've lately came across a few models where i needed to edit the rigging to make them work (humanoid), but every time I try to upload a model it gives me this error. Now I know most of the time it doesn't matter too much, but I've had models where I had to go back into blender and then it becomes a guessing game if I'm actually correct or not. So I'd love to see that the SDK actually shows the angle I need to edit instead of just giving me degrees without a point of reference. I hope this will be added in the future. This was Duloxetine and thank you for listening to my Ted Talk.",
